WEBVTT

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:04.060
<i>All that time, she,</i>

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:07.030
<i>Katou...</i>

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:39.960
Well then, let's go to the circle together, Katou.

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:45.690
It appears you completely fell for my feigned sleep.

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:46.700
Um,

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:50.030
you say that, but you actually were asleep, weren't you, Aki-kun?

00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:53.830
I meant to just pretend to sleep at first!

00:02:25.390 --> 00:02:27.960
What about Eriri and Kasumigaoka-senpai?

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:29.300
Not coming today!

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:32.030
Didn't I tell you?

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:33.640
Was that so?

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:35.310
All right, come here!

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:38.180
We're even using the broadcasting room?

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:40.310
Yeah, the circumstances require it.

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:50.500
A-Aki-kun?

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:10.930
You know, I actually meant to print this out,

00:03:10.930 --> 00:03:13.180
but my printer was all out of ink.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:15.470
Ah.

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:18.850
I guess there's that.

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:20.540
In other words,

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:26.370
showing things more in the raw, such as the heroine's vague attitude and her changing feelings,

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:32.510
is the core which makes for an even more appealing 2D heroine you really can love.

00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:35.090
Ah... I see.

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:38.120
In the game I originally planned,

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:41.010
fully highlighting the heroine's appeal,

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:45.600
turning you, Katou, into a heart-throbbing main heroine, was the end goal.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:47.170
H-Huh...

00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:52.130
But what we made in the end is completely different from that initial idea.

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:54.880
It was a grand and moving romance story.

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:58.570
Of course, I agreed to the changes,

00:03:58.570 --> 00:04:01.430
and with Utaha-senpai's and Eriri's skills,

00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:04.770
it was a huge success as a game.

00:04:04.770 --> 00:04:05.560
However...

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:07.700
Um, can I ask something?

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:09.270
What is it, Katou?

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:11.680
So, what is this document?

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:15.110
Katou, did you not read the title on the first page?

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:17.460
Um, that's not what I mean-

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:20.780
The project proposal for our next game, of course!

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:26.210
Why are you showing this to me?

00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:27.060
Katou!

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:29.040
You really didn't read it, did you?

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:31.340
This proposal from my soul!

00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:34.680
The main heroine will again be Kanou Meguri,

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:37.530
in other words, Katou Megumi!

00:04:37.530 --> 00:04:42.910
Do you seriously think I would definitely be happy to participate in that plan?

00:04:42.910 --> 00:04:44.450
I have no idea.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:45.520
I don't know.

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:46.810
However,

00:04:47.210 --> 00:04:50.610
without you on board, this project won't get anywhere.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:53.540
Even if all the others were there,

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:57.190
without you, we can't make this game.

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:01.660
I don't think you need to be that particular about that.

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:03.950
The model for the main heroine...

00:05:03.950 --> 00:05:09.130
It's such a vague, boring and ambiguous role...

00:05:09.130 --> 00:05:10.990
There are things I regret.

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:16.600
With the best possible members, we made the ultimate game.

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:18.680
Everybody did an amazing job.

00:05:19.010 --> 00:05:22.470
Eriri, Utaha-senpai and Michiru.

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:23.720
And you, too.

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:27.760
You gave your all until the very end.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:31.050
That's right, everybody did their best.

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:33.080
So it's fine now.

00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:35.570
There's no need to do anything more.

00:05:35.570 --> 00:05:39.320
But Katou, I haven't been able to take you to that place yet.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:41.370
That place?

00:05:41.830 --> 00:05:45.180
Beyond all of our hard work,

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:47.750
with thorough happiness and joy,

00:05:48.350 --> 00:05:50.460
but just a little bit of sadness...

00:05:50.460 --> 00:05:52.320
That catharsis.

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:56.680
I was the only one who didn't give it my all.

00:05:56.680 --> 00:05:59.280
I stopped pushing at the very last moment,

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:01.050
and stood still.

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:04.050
This is my revenge!

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:07.120
This time, I won't let you wake up from the dream!

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:09.450
I'll have you ride that high all the way!

00:06:09.450 --> 00:06:13.060
I'll make you unable to stop
making games or being an otaku!

00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:14.640
That's right!

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:16.500
The main heroine thing is just a bait-and-switch!

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:17.820
Nothing but a convenient excuse!

00:06:18.380 --> 00:06:22.660
I simply want to have fun with you at the after-party this time!

00:06:22.660 --> 00:06:24.740
And that's why... that's why...

00:06:24.740 --> 00:06:29.500
I have no choice but to create another plan in which you'll want to participate!

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:35.000
If that's the case, tell me,

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:39.830
why is your plan nothing but your cringy wild delusions?

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:44.280
Is this really meant to be a plan I'd want to participate in?

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:45.810
It's a revolution in gal games, right?

00:06:45.810 --> 00:06:48.640
I'm the only one who can pull off this plan, right?

00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:50.740
I wonder.

00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:54.010
What you want to do looks pretty ordinary to me.

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:57.520
Did you even read the proposal I wrote with my heart's blood?!

00:06:57.520 --> 00:06:59.290
The main idea of this plan is,

00:06:59.290 --> 00:07:04.220
we do what anyone could have thought of with the kind of depth and passion nobody could even imagine-

00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:05.540
That's the issue, Aki-kun.

00:07:05.540 --> 00:07:06.910
What is, Katou-kun?!

00:07:07.490 --> 00:07:08.240
Huh?

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:12.790
You're making such a grand game with this staff?

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:19.770
One person seems to be responsible for the plan, the scenario, and being the director,

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:21.050
or am I just imagining things?

00:07:21.050 --> 00:07:22.140
It's fine!

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:25.520
You'll be helping him with the plan and directing.

00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:27.550
What? No thanks, that's a pain.

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:32.290
Standing before a great project about to repaint the history of gal games is no place to feel bothered by such things!

00:07:32.290 --> 00:07:33.220
Aki-kun...

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:35.190
Please, Katou.

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:37.040
Once more,

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:38.460
just one more time,

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:42.820
become my main heroine, and the vice representative of the circle!

00:07:43.530 --> 00:07:47.270
I want you to take care of this circle together with me!

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:57.000
Can I confirm one thing?

00:07:57.410 --> 00:07:58.500
Yes.

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:03.410
Did you tell Eriri yet that you're making me the main heroine again?

00:08:03.410 --> 00:08:04.690
Not yet.

00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:06.510
Is that really okay?

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:09.320
Can you decide without asking Eriri?

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:12.270
Hey, Katou.

00:08:12.270 --> 00:08:15.770
I do know that this is extremely unlikely,

00:08:15.770 --> 00:08:19.090
but the reason you've been angry at me recently...

00:08:19.090 --> 00:08:24.670
Is it because you don't know what to think about me and Eriri having been so close lately,

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:29.530
or something else complicated like that, like in gal games?

00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:41.250
What are you saying, Aki-kun?

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:42.300
Of course not!

00:08:42.300 --> 00:08:43.180
Of course!

00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:44.630
Huh, what?

00:08:44.940 --> 00:08:49.420
Did you perhaps think that I might be in love with you,

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:52.510
completely oblivious to what it is that you have done to me?

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:55.120
But you know, it often happens in gal games!

00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:59.070
A heroine falling in love as time
goes by for no particular reason!

00:08:59.070 --> 00:09:05.900
Perhaps that's because they're made by people like you, who don't know much about 3D relationships.

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:07.970
Forgive me, stop flinging everything back at me!

00:09:07.970 --> 00:09:09.570
Hold back a little!

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:13.950
Huh, but if you say something that ridiculous...

00:09:15.730 --> 00:09:17.830
I'm really sorry, Katou.

00:09:17.830 --> 00:09:19.290
It's fine already.

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:21.840
I want to completely erase that from my memory.

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:23.440
No,

00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:25.750
I didn't mean this, but last year.

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:26.840
Last year?

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:30.020
Sorry I couldn't ask you for help.

00:09:30.020 --> 00:09:31.970
Sorry I couldn't rely on you.

00:09:31.970 --> 00:09:35.420
Sorry for... failing as a friend.

00:09:36.140 --> 00:09:37.180
That's...

00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:39.000
But thank you.

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:40.770
I'm so happy.

00:09:41.070 --> 00:09:42.120
What?

00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:42.900
Why?

00:09:42.900 --> 00:09:44.780
Because Katou,

00:09:44.780 --> 00:09:47.280
you love Blessing Software even more than I do!

00:09:48.300 --> 00:09:52.840
You love it so much that you can't forgive me for giving up on winter Comiket!

00:09:52.840 --> 00:09:56.590
That makes me so very, very happy!

00:09:57.620 --> 00:10:00.750
That's why I'm so very sorry.

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:16.090
Thank you, Katou.

00:10:16.090 --> 00:10:19.020
What...

00:10:19.920 --> 00:10:22.780
What are you talking about?

00:10:22.780 --> 00:10:24.330
Thank you.

00:10:24.330 --> 00:10:26.520
Thank you, Katou.

00:10:27.780 --> 00:10:28.950
And also...

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:31.120
I really am sorry.

00:10:31.780 --> 00:10:34.030
Sorry.

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:38.700
Sorry.

00:10:39.260 --> 00:10:40.220
Sorry.

00:10:43.980 --> 00:10:47.400
A-Aki-kun, you know,

00:10:47.400 --> 00:10:50.420
I've held it in all this time...

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:50.970
Sorry.

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:56.850
Just throwing "sorry" around cheaply like that isn't going to be enough!

00:10:56.850 --> 00:10:58.230
Well... yeah.

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:01.310
Why are you smiling?

00:11:01.310 --> 00:11:04.870
That'll just make me even more mad!

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:07.420
We're comrades, right?

00:11:07.420 --> 00:11:09.150
We're friends, right?

00:11:09.150 --> 00:11:12.990
Eriri and Kasumigaoka-senpai and Hyoudou-san too!

00:11:12.990 --> 00:11:14.900
Y-Yeah.

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:16.740
And me, too.

00:11:16.740 --> 00:11:24.330
And between friends, there are no secrets, no hidden things, and no decisions without talking about it, right?

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:29.990
Shouldn't you have talked with us about everything?

00:11:29.990 --> 00:11:31.080
Yeah,

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:32.590
you're right.

00:11:33.100 --> 00:11:34.700
I was in the wrong.

00:11:36.330 --> 00:11:38.550
I had fun.

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:41.770
I had more fun in the circle than I'd ever have thought.

00:11:41.770 --> 00:11:42.730
Katou...

00:11:42.730 --> 00:11:50.320
So these two months I've been apart from you and the others have been really hard.

00:11:50.320 --> 00:11:51.510
I'm sorry.

00:11:52.470 --> 00:11:53.740
I told you,

00:11:54.030 --> 00:11:57.620
your apologies don't have much weight.

00:12:01.640 --> 00:12:05.330
Do you really think the new system will work well?

00:12:05.650 --> 00:12:08.880
Of course, there may be problems at first,

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:10.590
but if we take it slow and get used to it...

00:12:10.590 --> 00:12:17.010
I mean, I think it's not possible for a novice like me to be the vice representative.

00:12:17.010 --> 00:12:20.010
All the other members are such amazing people.

00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:20.810
It'll be fine!

00:12:21.130 --> 00:12:23.890
The representative isn't that amazing anyway.

00:12:23.890 --> 00:12:25.410
Hmm...

00:12:25.410 --> 00:12:28.020
Sorry, could you pick up those onions?

00:12:28.020 --> 00:12:29.480
Why onions?

00:12:29.480 --> 00:12:30.740
Dinner.

00:12:30.740 --> 00:12:33.690
I figured curry would be a safe choice.

00:12:33.690 --> 00:12:35.320
You're making dinner?

00:12:35.320 --> 00:12:38.360
It seems like the meeting tonight will be long.

00:12:38.760 --> 00:12:41.160
It does?

00:12:41.940 --> 00:12:47.240
So you're asking Kasumigaoka-senpai for only the main route?

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:48.100
Yeah.

00:12:48.100 --> 00:12:50.620
Utaha-senpai has only just started university,

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:53.860
and she's also busy with writing her new light novel.

00:12:55.200 --> 00:12:59.050
Last year, when she supposedly was busy with university entrance exams and her light novel,

00:12:59.050 --> 00:13:02.290
she did do a full game, though.

00:13:02.290 --> 00:13:05.060
B-But even if it's just one route,

00:13:05.060 --> 00:13:08.800
I expect Kasumi Utako's best work from her!

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:12.080
But if you do the rest of the scenario,

00:13:12.080 --> 00:13:14.940
don't you think there'll be a huge gap in quality?

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:17.320
We can only be optimistic about it now, right?!

00:13:17.320 --> 00:13:21.570
Well, I guess the representative just has to do his best about it.

00:13:22.040 --> 00:13:24.770
All right, I'll go buy these.

00:13:24.770 --> 00:13:27.030
Lend me some casual wear, okay?

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:29.420
You're just assuming you'll stay overnight?

00:13:31.860 --> 00:13:35.640
So is Eriri still in a slump?

00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:36.460
Yeah.

00:13:36.460 --> 00:13:41.020
So I think it'd be difficult to have her do the art for all the characters at this point.

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:46.310
But if you were to include another artist,

00:13:46.310 --> 00:13:54.770
is there anybody else who's about as good as Eriri, not in any other circle, and whom you could ask to join?

00:13:54.770 --> 00:13:58.430
Thanks for making me realise the harsh reality.

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:01.660
Are your parents home today?

00:14:01.660 --> 00:14:04.920
They're actually in Nagano, at a relative's memorial service,

00:14:04.920 --> 00:14:07.490
staying today and tomorrow overnight.

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:10.160
Huh, so it's the same pattern again?

00:14:11.380 --> 00:14:13.350
Coming in!

00:14:14.680 --> 00:14:17.960
You seriously don't worry about anything.

00:14:19.270 --> 00:14:20.840
I said it earlier, too,

00:14:20.840 --> 00:14:25.100
but our Cherry Blessing really became an amazing game.

00:14:25.100 --> 00:14:31.150
But it was not because my plan, the game I wanted to make, was amazing.

00:14:31.150 --> 00:14:36.360
Well, Kasumigaoka-senpai and Eriri pretty much carried you there.

00:14:37.060 --> 00:14:41.740
So for our next game, we're going back to Blessing Software's roots.

00:14:41.740 --> 00:14:42.740
Huh...

00:14:42.740 --> 00:14:46.150
We make a game which finds the appeal in carefree everyday moments.

00:14:46.150 --> 00:14:47.080
That so?

00:14:47.080 --> 00:14:51.960
The characters will be more moe than in the previous game, but moving people with such a normal story,

00:14:51.960 --> 00:14:54.600
we catch the players with your true appeal-

00:14:54.600 --> 00:14:55.870
What do you think?

00:15:03.340 --> 00:15:04.680
It's fine, isn't it?

00:15:05.590 --> 00:15:12.190
The kinds of games which focus on communicating with the heroines often rely on the system, right?

00:15:12.190 --> 00:15:15.190
You manage the health and the schedule of the main character,

00:15:15.190 --> 00:15:18.090
choose the place for the date and your present from three options,

00:15:18.090 --> 00:15:20.790
kiss the girls by touching the screen...

00:15:20.790 --> 00:15:23.110
Is that so? Sounds nice.

00:15:24.300 --> 00:15:26.860
That's of course great too.

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:31.530
But I want to do a story-heavy adventure game instead.

00:15:31.530 --> 00:15:34.700
I feel like that would give it an Aki Tomoya vibe.

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:36.050
What do you think, Katou?

00:15:36.050 --> 00:15:37.920
Well, I wonder...

00:15:37.920 --> 00:15:39.520
Hey, this is important!

00:15:39.520 --> 00:15:43.300
I love stories with girls I love in them!

00:15:43.300 --> 00:15:47.460
When it comes to 2D, you're not
embarrassed at all, are you, Aki-kun?

00:15:48.140 --> 00:15:49.560
Just listen.

00:15:49.560 --> 00:15:51.030
Listen for now.

00:15:51.030 --> 00:15:51.890
Sure, sure.

00:15:52.200 --> 00:15:53.820
It certainly is difficult.

00:15:53.820 --> 00:15:56.270
It may end up done worse than our previous game.

00:15:56.650 --> 00:15:58.020
It may not sell that well.

00:15:58.020 --> 00:15:59.840
It may get crushed.

00:15:59.840 --> 00:16:01.650
But even so, I-

00:16:02.170 --> 00:16:03.280
Grain of rice.

00:16:03.610 --> 00:16:05.560
Y-Yeah...

00:16:08.510 --> 00:16:10.540
The game part will be a bit like this.

00:16:10.540 --> 00:16:12.870
So a normal school gal game?

00:16:12.870 --> 00:16:18.460
That's right, there'll be no memories from a previous life, incurable illnesses, time leaps or parallel world stuff.

00:16:18.460 --> 00:16:22.720
It fights with casual conversation, everyday events, and the cuteness of the heroines.

00:16:22.720 --> 00:16:27.210
But hasn't that already been done in this and other games?

00:16:27.210 --> 00:16:31.140
No, this game doesn't reach my ideal in certain ways.

00:16:31.140 --> 00:16:32.780
Two ways, actually.

00:16:32.780 --> 00:16:34.140
Huh...

00:16:34.140 --> 00:16:36.250
First of all, casual conversations.

00:16:36.250 --> 00:16:40.030
Even though the game is mostly comprised of conversation scenes between the main character and the heroines,

00:16:40.030 --> 00:16:44.080
they're extremely boring, dull, tedious, and utterly pointless.

00:16:44.080 --> 00:16:46.990
We all have to be careful about that.

00:16:46.990 --> 00:16:49.040
And secondly, the heroines' reactions.

00:16:49.040 --> 00:16:50.930
It's way too repetitive!

00:16:50.930 --> 00:16:53.280
Tsundere! Little sister! Older sister!

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:55.690
They're just doing the same tropes over and over again!

00:16:55.690 --> 00:16:58.960
But didn't you say tropes are important?

00:16:58.960 --> 00:17:01.000
Yes, they are, extremely so!

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:03.210
But you know, Katou, heroines are people!

00:17:03.640 --> 00:17:09.290
Their reactions should change based on the time they've spent together with you and how they feel in that moment.

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:11.280
Your attitude would change when you fall in love, right?

00:17:11.280 --> 00:17:13.760
You'd speak differently when you've
known each other for a long time, right?

00:17:13.760 --> 00:17:15.950
Subtly and gradually!

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:17.980
Indeed, you can't change it all at once, either!

00:17:17.980 --> 00:17:19.810
That'll break the players' immersion!

00:17:19.810 --> 00:17:21.970
That's why changing it little by little,

00:17:21.970 --> 00:17:23.240
with great variation,

00:17:23.240 --> 00:17:26.310
we express the heroines' appeal as human beings-

00:17:26.910 --> 00:17:28.030
Katou?

00:17:28.030 --> 00:17:29.130
Aki-kun...

00:17:29.130 --> 00:17:30.740
Y-Yes?

00:17:30.740 --> 00:17:33.220
Sit there.

00:17:33.220 --> 00:17:35.580
I-I am sitting.

00:17:36.140 --> 00:17:40.110
Aki-kun, like you say, relationships change!

00:17:40.110 --> 00:17:41.470
Y-Yes?

00:17:41.470 --> 00:17:44.470
I think you have to change your attitude and the way you act,

00:17:44.470 --> 00:17:48.010
based on the time you've spent together and how you feel about them.

00:17:48.010 --> 00:17:54.950
So I want to question you behaving and speaking the same way in winter Comiket as before.

00:17:54.950 --> 00:17:58.890
If you know it that well, why didn't you do it for me?

00:17:59.210 --> 00:18:02.450
Aren't we close enough for you to understand how I feel?

00:18:02.450 --> 00:18:04.980
I-I thought you forgave me for that already?

00:18:04.980 --> 00:18:09.380
I got mad because I realised that you don't understand it at all!

00:18:09.380 --> 00:18:10.310
Wait a moment!

00:18:10.310 --> 00:18:11.990
Calm down, Katou!

00:18:11.990 --> 00:18:14.850
You said that heroines in games are human too, right?

00:18:14.850 --> 00:18:16.630
That's right, that's exactly so!

00:18:16.630 --> 00:18:20.250
Even me, the main heroine, is a human!

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:22.840
I think I'll cry again.

00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:27.640
What's with this "How to Raise a Boring Heroine"?!

00:18:27.640 --> 00:18:30.760
You have said that my character is completely dead,

00:18:30.760 --> 00:18:33.780
but I had no idea you'd even put it in the title!

00:18:33.780 --> 00:18:35.760
I'll go with something else if you don't like it!

00:18:36.560 --> 00:18:38.270
So you know,

00:18:38.270 --> 00:18:41.740
if you can't even read my reactions,

00:18:41.740 --> 00:18:46.150
do you really think you can make such a delicate game?

00:18:46.150 --> 00:18:51.280
<i>Well, at this stage, the only thing I can do is say that I'll do my best.</i>

00:18:51.280 --> 00:18:52.930
Your efforts aside,

00:18:52.930 --> 00:18:56.200
perhaps you completely lack the sense for it.

00:18:56.200 --> 00:18:59.160
<i>I-I will study the topic!</i>

00:18:59.160 --> 00:19:05.020
You know, isn't what you want to do here in a sense a lot more difficult than our previous game?

00:19:05.020 --> 00:19:07.420
<i>W-Well, more importantly, Katou.</i>

00:19:07.420 --> 00:19:08.960
What is it?

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:12.140
<i>Since you wanted to take a bath to calm your feelings,</i>

00:19:12.140 --> 00:19:15.680
<i>you should just enjoy it without preaching to me...</i>

00:19:15.680 --> 00:19:18.970
Sheesh, shut up!

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:21.450
<i>Whose fault is it that we're in this situation anyway?!</i>

00:19:21.450 --> 00:19:22.300
Sorry.

00:19:22.300 --> 00:19:26.650
<i>And I'm telling you, your "sorry" doesn't have much weight today, Aki-kun!</i>

00:19:26.650 --> 00:19:27.480
Sorry about that.

00:19:27.480 --> 00:19:28.980
<i>Sheesh!</i>

00:19:28.980 --> 00:19:33.580
<i>It's not like I wanted to take my phone to the bath with me!</i>

00:19:36.870 --> 00:19:40.090
So, what are you going to do?

00:19:40.090 --> 00:19:43.370
I guess I'll have to first persuade the other members.

00:19:43.830 --> 00:19:49.460
I wonder if Kasumigaoka-senpai will participate even now that she's graduated.

00:19:49.460 --> 00:19:52.470
I guess I can begin by showing her my sincerity.

00:19:52.470 --> 00:19:55.210
Do you mean you'll confess to her?

00:19:55.210 --> 00:19:57.220
Sleep already, Katou-san.

00:19:57.220 --> 00:20:02.200
Besides, how will you handle Eriri's slump?

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:03.610
I guess...

00:20:04.340 --> 00:20:06.780
...I'll just have to give it time.

00:20:07.470 --> 00:20:11.110
Do you really think that time will solve it?

00:20:11.110 --> 00:20:13.010
I don't know,

00:20:13.010 --> 00:20:16.250
but I don't know what else I could do, either.

00:20:16.250 --> 00:20:20.660
Should you concentrate on me like this when you don't know that yet?

00:20:20.660 --> 00:20:21.910
Sleep already.

00:20:21.910 --> 00:20:24.370
I don't know about that!

00:20:24.980 --> 00:20:27.750
So what should I do, then?

00:20:27.790 --> 00:20:30.500
I don't know either!

00:20:30.500 --> 00:20:31.910
Sheesh.

00:20:31.910 --> 00:20:34.630
You're all over the place today, Katou.

00:20:35.240 --> 00:20:36.630
You're right.

00:20:37.910 --> 00:20:39.630
Hey, Aki-kun.

00:20:39.630 --> 00:20:40.640
What is it?

00:20:41.350 --> 00:20:45.760
Forget about how I am now by tomorrow.

00:20:45.760 --> 00:20:48.150
Yeah, I know.

00:20:48.430 --> 00:20:50.320
No way, though.

00:20:50.320 --> 00:20:51.770
Ah, that's right.

00:20:54.070 --> 00:20:55.590
What now?

00:20:56.370 --> 00:20:57.950
Here, Aki-kun.

00:20:57.950 --> 00:21:00.330
It's of course obligatory,

00:21:00.330 --> 00:21:01.530
but anyway, okay?

00:21:01.530 --> 00:21:03.520
Thanks for that!

00:21:03.520 --> 00:21:05.900
All right, I'll sleep for real now.

00:21:05.900 --> 00:21:06.740
Yeah.

00:21:18.120 --> 00:21:19.390
Good night.
